source: crates/escher-cli/tests/cli/usage.rs
expression: "snapshot(&[\"render\", \"-h\"])"
---
status: Success
--- stdout
Render the tiling of a signature in orbifold notation and write it to a PNG file

Usage: escher render [OPTIONS] --output <FILE> <SIGNATURE>

Arguments:
  <SIGNATURE>  The signature in orbifold notation, such as *632. In a POSIX shell, put a signature that contains *, (, or ) in single quotes, as in '2*(12)'

Options:
  -o, --output <FILE>              The PNG file to write. An existing file is replaced
      --size <WIDTHxHEIGHT>        The image size in pixels, as WIDTHxHEIGHT [default: 512x512]
      --colouring <COLOURING>      One colour for every tile, parity for the colouring with two colours in which no two neighbouring tiles share a colour, or the id of a colouring that the command info --colourings lists, such as 4a. The default is parity when the tiling has it, and one otherwise
      --colours <COLOURS>          The fill colours, separated by commas, one for each colour of the colouring, each as #rgb, #rrggbb, or image:FILE for a PNG image painted over the mask of that colour that render-masks writes. The default takes the first colours of a built-in list of 12. In a POSIX shell, put the colours in single quotes, as in '#e9c46a,image:fill-1.png'
      --wythoff <MARKS>            Draw the Wythoff construction of a reflection triangle instead of its tiles, as three digits, one for each corner of the signature in the order that info prints, where 1 turns on the mirror opposite that corner, such as 010 for the regular tiling {7,3} of *732. --colours then gives one colour for each face type, in the order of the corners
      --border-width <WIDTH>       The border width, in the unit of --border-unit. 0 draws no border. The default is 1 for pixels and 0.05 for intrinsic
      --border-unit <UNIT>         The unit of --border-width: pixels of the image, or intrinsic for a length in the geometry of the tiling, such as 0.05 [default: pixels] [possible values: pixels, intrinsic]
      --border-colour <COLOUR>     The border colour, as #rgb or #rrggbb [default: #000000]
      --samples <N>                The number of samples along each side of a pixel. The pixel averages N by N samples [default: 4]
      --max-folds <N>              The largest number of folds of one sample. A sample that needs more takes the border colour [default: 1500]
      --background <COLOUR>        The colour outside the model of a hyperbolic tiling or the ball of a spherical tiling, and where an image fill is transparent or has no pixel, as #rgb or #rrggbb [default: #ffffff]
      --threads <N>                The number of threads, from 1 to 256. The default is the available parallelism, at most 256
      --stats                      Print statistics of the rendering to standard output
      --set <NAME=VALUE>           Set a shape parameter of the tiles, as NAME=VALUE, such as aspect=1.5, once for each parameter. --help lists the parameters, and info <SIGNATURE> prints those of a signature
      --model <MODEL>              The model in which a hyperbolic tiling is drawn: the Poincare disk, the upper half-plane, the band, or the Klein disk [default: disk] [possible values: disk, half-plane, band, klein]
      --rotation <YAW,PITCH,ROLL>  The rotation of the ball of a spherical tiling, as three angles in degrees. YAW turns the front of the ball to the right, PITCH turns it up, and ROLL turns the image counterclockwise, in this order [default: 0,0,0]
      --light <X,Y,Z>              The direction from the ball of a spherical tiling to the light, as X,Y,Z, with X to the right, Y up, and Z toward the viewer. The length is ignored [default: -1,1,2]
      --shading <SHADING>          Phong shading of the ball of a spherical tiling, or none [default: phong] [possible values: phong, none]
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')
--- stderr
--- end
